%N A071484 Sprague-Grundy values for octal game .3037.
%C A071484 Octal games .206 and .216 have values a(n-1). - _Eric M. Schmidt_, Feb 09 2017
%C A071484 From _Tyler Satchel Orden_, Jul 30 2026: (Start)
%C A071484 a(n) is also the Sprague-Grundy value of a heap of n+1 tokens in the octal game .206; equivalently, the Sprague-Grundy sequence of .206 is 0, 0, followed by this sequence.
%C A071484 Computed (as the game .206) through heap size 2^30 = 1073741824 by Tyler Satchel Orden (2026), extending A. Flammenkamp's tables for .206, which reached 2^29: 10339 rare values in Flammenkamp's sparse-space sense, the last at heap size 5668113; the maximum value grows to 847, first attained at heap size 811850921. Flammenkamp's published invariants at 2^29 were reproduced exactly before extending. (End)
%D A071484 E. R. Berlekamp, J. H. Conway and R. K. Guy, Winning Ways, Academic Press, NY, 2 vols., 1982; see Chapter 4.
